  "reasoning": "The patient presents with calf cramps, difficulty walking, and fatigue after working, attributing it to obesity. These symptoms are characteristic of venous insufficiency and varicose veins, which commonly cause leg cramps, aching, heaviness, and tiredness in the lower limbs, especially in obese individuals or those who stand for prolonged periods. Other potential diagnoses like arthritis typically involve joint swelling and stiffness rather than isolated calf cramps; diabetes presents with systemic metabolic symptoms like excessive thirst and urination; and infectious diseases like malaria or dengue would include fever and chills. Given the localized lower limb symptoms and the risk factor of obesity, varicose veins is the most consistent diagnosis supported by the clinical picture and reference patterns.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]varicose veins[/DIAGNOSIS]"
}

